        "procedure": "SI general procedure (main text only states that Ln(NO3)3·6H2O, H8TBC8A and PhPO3H2 in basic DMF–CH3OH (1:1, v/v) at 130 °C give colorless plates, without reagent amounts). A mixture of H8TBC8A (0.05 mmol, 65 mg), PhPO3H2 (0.1 mmol, 16 mg) and PrCl3·6H2O (0.28 mmol, 100 mg) in DMF/CH3OH/NEt3 (5/5/1 mL) was stirred for 10 min, sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined bomb, heated at 130 °C for 3 days and cooled over 1 day to room temperature. Colorless plate crystals were isolated by filtration, washed with DMF/CH3OH (1:1, v/v) and air-dried. Formate is described in the main text as arising from DMF decarbonylation and bicarbonate from atmospheric CO2.",
